{"id": "EUVD-2026-81915", "enisaUuid": "6ef4d0ee-fc38-316e-a8c6-3d6d61a9a26d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: fix corruption of urgent data on multi-segment retransmit\n\nOn the normal xmit path, while in urgent mode we refuse to build a\nmulti-segment TSO packet, so every segment gets its own urg_ptr:\n\n\t/* tcp_write_xmit() */\n\tlimit = mss_now;\n\tif (tso_segs > 1 && !tcp_urg_mode(tp))\n\t\tlimit = tcp_mss_split_point(...);\n\nThe retransmit path has no such guard. __tcp_retransmit_skb() builds a\nsegs > 1 skb and hands it to the GSO layer, which only advances th->seq\nper segment and copies urg_ptr verbatim:\n\n\t/* __tcp_retransmit_skb() */\n\tlen = cur_mss * segs;\t\t/* segs > 1, no urg_mode check */\n\t...\n\t/* tcp_gso_segment(): bumps seq only, urg_ptr is copied */\n\nurg_ptr is an offset from the segment's own seq, so a copied value points\nat a different place on each segment. The receiver rebuilds the absolute\nurgent seq as seg.seq + urg_ptr, so it walks a moving urgent point instead\nof the one OOB byte:\n\n\tseg1  seq 1     urg_ptr 5001 -> urgent @ 5001   (ok)\n\tseg2  seq 1001  urg_ptr 5001 -> urgent @ 6001   (wrong, +MSS)\n\tseg3  seq 2001  urg_ptr 5001 -> urgent @ 7001   (wrong, +2*MSS)\n\nThe real OOB byte is never pointed at, so the receiver stops splicing it\nout and delivers it as normal in-band data, corrupting the stream.\n\nGuard the retransmit length like the xmit path: keep segs = 1 while in\nurgent mode.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:05:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:57:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8eb51013b6308870479a64b4a2a018697b997849", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/711bfd762bec05fb19bc3b17cbb157c39f4e66da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d4e005c198dc410ad568f832bffa7569c059ff8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4fd2ee4ac154c204d95d8db72221446dac5af9b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ebe55406404f3cb28e36d2b668e2c6c05026ec29", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8f08a94b2a4addc39249dcf9c792e786108621b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47eb90299e6882d6445672530dd7c51ac33ebdbd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce2b807f42ed5e55567b8864ab72963f90779270"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90054", "GHSA-cwq3-366f-g758"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00350009-d66a-3db9-9725-457a929e0d3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "1125778c-d8a9-3ed3-a4ea-76caac359d24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10d3be569243def8d92ac3722395ef5a59c504e6 <47eb90299e6882d6445672530dd7c51ac33ebdbd"}, {"id": "1782ada7-b6ee-33a0-993e-29003e626ad1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3541f4ac-4155-3cd0-abc3-2d2275e86c89", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "50396eda-d72b-355a-b45c-8ae20b920468", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10d3be569243def8d92ac3722395ef5a59c504e6 <3d4e005c198dc410ad568f832bffa7569c059ff8"}, {"id": "5124f72f-6e2b-3459-86c5-28fe3de8d603", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "560ca456-0963-3f53-aac8-c0d0a487adeb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "56219ca3-d627-3b11-839e-2ccb5589138c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.7"}, {"id": "68e8a311-f065-368a-9a5f-9d6d88d450b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10d3be569243def8d92ac3722395ef5a59c504e6 <711bfd762bec05fb19bc3b17cbb157c39f4e66da"}, {"id": "807ccd16-cff9-354c-8f5a-684f55808ea8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "b176fa32-881e-3eb6